- Article 5(1)(c) addresses social scoring over time that leads to detrimental treatment in unrelated contexts or treatment that is unjustified or disproportionate. Whether the system produces such scores, and the context and proportionality of any resulting treatment, are needed to establish the connection to this rule. [Article 5(1)(c)]
